+// Padded GQA-6 fold for the RDNA3_0 native-Q8_0 decode/verify band -- OPT-IN, default OFF.
+// It replaces the tile launcher's three KV-head traversals per query row (ncols2 = 2 for a ratio of 6)
+// with one padded eight-column block (ncols1 = 1, ncols2 = 8; columns 6/7 carry zero Q and are never
+// stored).  It is NOT a padded-column bookkeeping change only: the pin moves cols_per_block, so
+// ntiles_z_gqa 3 -> 1 and the kernel's occupancy (max_blocks_per_sm 18 -> 6), and the launcher's split
+// search therefore picks a different parallel_blocks P (measured on gfx1100 at a 32K cache: 18 -> 6).
+// Block b owns KV iterations b, b+P, ... and the combine sums the P partials in block order, so P IS the
+// summation order -- greedy text moves at near-ties (GREEDY-PURITY.md 99, 104; the point reads mean KLD
+// 0.000001 / same-top-p 100.000 % at the decode width, so it is rounding-level, not approximate).
+// That is why the default is the r359 path -- GGML_HIP_FA_TILE_GQA6_FOLD=1 is the opt-in -- and why the
+// value is read once per process.
 static inline bool ggml_cuda_fattn_tile_gqa6_fold_enabled() {
     static const bool enabled = [] {
